[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Actor Lifecycle, Spawning, and Destruction in Unreal Engine"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Understanding the Actor lifecycle is crucial for developing performant and bug-free games in Unreal Engine. Every Actor goes through a predictable sequence of events from the moment it is instantiated in memory to the moment it is garbage collected."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"The Major Phases of an Actor's Lifecycle"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Instantiation: Memory is allocated via SpawnActor, and the class constructor runs."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Initialization: Components are created, and default properties are applied."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Registration: Components are registered with the physics and rendering scenes."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Play: BeginPlay is called, signaling the start of active simulation."},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Tick: Every frame, Tick is called to update behavior and logic."},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Destruction: EndPlay is called, followed by unregistration and garbage collection."},{"order":10,"type":"subheading","text":"Spawning Actors in C++"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"To spawn an Actor dynamically during gameplay in C++, you utilize the UWorld::SpawnActor function. You must provide the class you wish to spawn, along with a transform representing the location and rotation."},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"FActorSpawnParameters SpawnParams;
SpawnParams.Owner = this;
SpawnParams.SpawnCollisionHandlingOverride = ESpawnActorCollisionHandlingMethod::AlwaysSpawn;

FVector SpawnLocation = FVector(0.0f, 0.0f, 500.0f);
FRotator SpawnRotation = FRotator::ZeroRotator;

AMyCustomActor* SpawnedActor = GetWorld()->SpawnActor<AMyCustomActor>(AMyCustomActor::StaticClass(), SpawnLocation, SpawnRotation, SpawnParams);"},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"Destruction and Cleanup"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"When an Actor is no longer needed, you should explicitly destroy it using the Destroy function. This triggers the EndPlay event, allowing the Actor to clean up timers, unbind delegates, and release resources safely before it is fully removed."},{"order":15,"type":"code","text":"if (TargetActor && TargetActor->IsValidLowLevel())
{
    bool bSuccess = TargetActor->Destroy();
    if (bSuccess)
    {
        UE_LOG(LogTemp, Warning, TEXT("Actor successfully destroyed."));
    }
}"}]
